      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with a lovely spring day ahead, blue skies and light wind after groomers laid down a full spread of cord for excellent on-trail turns. Cold overnight temperatures mean off-trail will be firm at first, softening with the sunshine; the natural base holds at 150 cm at the top of Home Basin, with no new snowfall in the past 24 hours. It's currently -6°C with light winds around 13 km/h gusting to 23 km/h. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and the Beginner Platter are all open, all 3 of 3 lifts running; 7 of 9 terrain zones are open including Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Saddle Basin and Summit Slopes, with Matukituki Basin delayed and Motatapu Chutes closed. Backcountry and skinning access are both open; the access road is chain-free but chains must always be carried, with an active road hazard advisory and a free shuttle running from the bottom of the access road. Five days remain in the season. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
